<title>BANGLADESH: Bata Shoe company pays 22 taka dividend for 1996.</title>
<headline>Bata Shoe company pays 22 taka dividend for 1996.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year 1996.</p>
<p>			(In million taka unless stated)</p>
<p>				   1996		     1995</p>
<p>    Turnover		  1.96 billion    vs	  1.95 billion</p>
<p>    Gross profit	     722		vs	  671</p>
<p>    Profit before tax	224		vs	  163</p>
<p>    Profit after tax	 130		vs	  135</p>
<p>Profit available for</p>
<p>    appropriation	    460		vs	   396</p>
<p>    Dividend	    22 taka on 10-taka share vs 3.0 taka</p>
<p>Note: Bata Shoe Company (Bangladesh Ltd), 70 percent of which is owned by Northern Investment Co. Ltd of Canada, held its annual general meeting on Tuesday. The meeting was told that the gross profit rose substantially because of reduction of sales expenses.</p>
</text>
